From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 13:20:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 45/62] verimark: log pre/post getlist counts at
 ENR_S_RESOLVE_TUID for IT diagnose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Verify on the IT consistently returns status 0x0905 from 0x99
match even after a re-enroll that fprintd reports as completed.
Hypothesis : our skip of 0x96 03 commit on the IT means the
template is never actually written to the sensor's NVRAM —
post_list.count would then equal pre_list.count, and the resolve
loop would leave effective_tuid unchanged.

Log pre_count, post_count, and the first 8 bytes of effective_tuid
so we can confirm whether the enroll actually grew the on-sensor
template set or not.

TEMP.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index 1996067..c9dc34a 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2607,6 +2607,7 @@ enroll_sm_run_state(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
             cancel, enr_cb_getlist_post, ssm);
         return;
     case ENR_S_RESOLVE_TUID: {
+        gboolean found_new = FALSE;
         for (uint8_t i = 0; i < ctx->post_list.count; i++) {
             gboolean in_pre = FALSE;
             for (uint8_t j = 0; j < ctx->pre_list.count; j++) {
@@ -2627,9 +2628,21 @@ enroll_sm_run_state(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
                             "using device-reported storage_handle for "
                             "FpPrint match later");
                 }
+                found_new = TRUE;
                 break;
             }
         }
+        /* TEMP diag : confirm the template was actually persisted on the
+         * sensor by checking that getlist post-enroll grew vs pre-enroll. */
+        fp_warn("enroll: RESOLVE_TUID — pre_count=%u post_count=%u found_new=%d, "
+                "effective_tuid[0..8] = %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x %02x",
+                (unsigned)ctx->pre_list.count,
+                (unsigned)ctx->post_list.count,
+                (int)found_new,
+                ctx->effective_tuid[0], ctx->effective_tuid[1],
+                ctx->effective_tuid[2], ctx->effective_tuid[3],
+                ctx->effective_tuid[4], ctx->effective_tuid[5],
+                ctx->effective_tuid[6], ctx->effective_tuid[7]);
         fpi_ssm_mark_completed(ssm);
         return;
     }
